Test band, DOS and complete PW wavefunction output for norm-conserving Si.

The original six Max_wfc fingerprints used the largest absolute real or
imaginary component at the first k-point, rounded to four decimals. A global
complex phase changes this quantity, while errors in other coefficients or
k-points can leave it unchanged. This fixture instead stores both complete
k-point wavefunctions under wfc_pw.ref and compares every complex coefficient
after fitting one global phase per nondegenerate band. No vector is
renormalized. The collector checks all G vectors, metadata, finite values,
normalization and mutual orthogonality. A degenerate spectrum is rejected
because it requires a separately validated subspace comparison.

The full-coefficient and Gram-entry limits are 1e-7. The existing band-energy
limit remains 1e-8 eV; energy, force-sum and stress-sum acceptance limits remain
1e-7 eV, 1e-4 eV/Angstrom and 1e-3 kbar. The complete-wavefunction boolean
replaces six phase-sensitive scalar fingerprints; all other property checks
remain. A missing complete reference causes failure.

The INPUT retains the default CG solver, original structure, pseudopotential,
20 Ry wavefunction cutoff, six bands, k-points, smearing, initial-density
choice and random seed. Numerical controls use real-space SCF threshold
1e-11, initial/maximum inner threshold 1e-18, budgets of 200 SCF and 500 inner
iterations, and disabled empty-band threshold smoothing. Band output uses
16 decimal places. PW text coefficients now retain 17 significant digits.

The references were generated by a separate converged CG MPI4 calculation
on 2026-10-29 using the corrected CG gradient projection and stable energy
change. The executable SHA-256 was:
625c9df20c3363232e9fd0eb742b9037869c318adf33e865b984d1b84be980a3
GNU 12.3, OpenMPI 5.0.10, CPU Release, one OpenMP/OpenBLAS/MKL thread.

Fresh CG, Davidson and PPCG runs at each of 1, 2 and 4 MPI ranks all converged
in SCF and passed all 90 property checks. All 36 pairwise complete-wavefunction
comparisons passed. Maximum differences were 4.664e-9 per complex coefficient,
3.828e-10 eV per band energy, 1.308e-12 eV in total energy, 4.001e-10 eV/Angstrom
per force component and 1.883e-7 kbar per stress component. The largest Gram
error was 1.821e-14.

The shared 1e-18 input has solver-dependent meaning: energy change for CG and
Davidson, residual for PPCG with its existing numerical floor. The PPCG runs
retained 17, 20 and 18 early-iteration residual warnings at 1, 2 and 4 ranks,
respectively. None occurred at the final electronic step. These diagnostics
remain recorded alongside the passing output comparisons.

To reproduce, use clean copies with ks_solver=cg, dav and ppcg and run
Autotest.sh at -n1/-n2/-n4 with -o1. The full-wavefunction comparator has 32
positive/corruption tests, including phase changes, hidden relative-phase
errors, missing k-points, malformed data and missing reference files.
